Suggests: tesseract-ocr
Provides: superdot
Conflicts: superdot
Replaces: superdot
Description: Clipboard, emoji and more Windows shortcuts for Linux: Win+V, Win+. and more
 SuperV brings two Windows panels to Linux. Super+V shows the last 25
 things you copied (text and images): pick one to paste it into the app
 you are using, pin favourites, clear the rest. Super+. opens the emoji
 panel: type to search emoji, kaomoji and symbols, and the one you pick is
 typed where you were writing. Ctrl+Super+Alt+V pastes as plain text,
 Super+Shift+C picks a colour on screen, Super+Shift+T copies text from the
 screen (with tesseract-ocr). Each can be turned off. Works on GNOME, KDE
 Plasma, Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce, on Wayland and X11. Never connects to the
 internet.
 .
 Replaces SuperDot, which is now part of SuperV.
